405 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (HEALTH ENERGY INTERVENTION IN RI-BHOI  Since 2022, MOSONiE Socio-Economic Foundation has been conducting comprehensive physical solar monitoring across 49 health centers in 4 blocks of Ri-Bhoi District, Meghalaya. The initiative aims to assess and document performance gaps in solar energy systems installed at these centers, ensuring reliable power for essential healthcare services. As part of this ongoing effort, MOSONiE-SEF, in partnership with SELCO Foundation, conducted Community Sensitization and Asset Ownership Meetings at Mawlyndep HWC in Umsning Block and Mawdem CHC in Jirang Block. The meetings aimed to introduce communities to the solar systems installed in their health centers, promote awareness about the importance of uninterrupted solar power for healthcare, and encourage local ownership for long-term sustainability. Participants included village heads, school teachers, healthcare workers, and residents and expressed interest in supporting the upkeep of the solar infrastructure. Key Action Points Moving Forward:)
/E (HEALTH ENERGY INTERVENTION IN RI-BHOI  Since 2022, MOSONiE Socio-Economic Foundation has been conducting comprehensive physical solar monitoring across 49 health centers in 4 blocks of Ri-Bhoi District, Meghalaya. The initiative aims to assess and document performance gaps in solar energy systems installed at these centers, ensuring reliable power for essential healthcare services. As part of this ongoing effort, MOSONiE-SEF, in partnership with SELCO Foundation, conducted Community Sensitization and Asset Ownership Meetings at Mawlyndep HWC in Umsning Block and Mawdem CHC in Jirang Block. The meetings aimed to introduce communities to the solar systems installed in their health centers, promote awareness about the importance of uninterrupted solar power for healthcare, and encourage local ownership for long-term sustainability. Participants included village heads, school teachers, healthcare workers, and residents and expressed interest in supporting the upkeep of the solar infrastructure. Key Action Points Moving Forward:)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
